id: pm-rl-measured-influence
title: Measure evaluation sensitivity to declared training slices
description: "Run explicitly budgeted omission and integer reweighting experiments for declared training slices; retain exact checkpoints and measured per-evaluation associations, and carry bounded evidence into the next proposal."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: evaluation,influence,training
created_at: "2026-10-29T08:20:10.275Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T10:39:04.942Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Reports reproduce on a fixed learner and seed; Held-out data never enters training; Exhausted experiment budgets return partial evidence without a ranking claim; Typed SDK and compact CLI output, audit records, recursive proposal evidence, non-git public-copy validation, seeded model tests and npm plus Bun release gates"
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T08:20:18.810Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current core CLI/SDK, pm-rl policy-card.ts and evaluation-plan.ts, and pm-jev counterfactual.ts. Core owns native records/history/locks; policy cards explain provenance and validity; Jev removes inference evidence. This feature measures retraining sensitivity. Preserve all normal proposal, evaluation, promotion and feedback gates. Results remain associations; no causal identification claim. Current published CLI is 2026.10.28; package SDK remains pinned 2026.10.25."
  "2026-10-29T08:28:28.000Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the first typed request/report schema and fixed seeded retraining using the existing bandit kernel. Integer multiplicities implement omissions/reweighting; exact integer budgets include the baseline. Numerical tests confirm deterministic checkpoints, changed held-out scores without changed fitted parameters, strict dense/finite admission, and partial evidence with ranking=null. Native report identity is immutable; proposal evidence cites a certified SDK history revision and is retained in seed/candidate provenance. No shared experiment budget, plan replay or new promotion authority is introduced."
  "2026-10-29T08:46:27.483Z",codex-agent,"Public-copy validation passed on unbraind/pm-ops at ba05bb8b96b313b86d25896ef40880712f295881: 162 items, 116 training, 46 held out, 42 held-out done-role items (SDK registry semantics). Four fits used 2048 samples and 32 updates; overall expected-reward deltas were +0.004185111930395058, -0.003866597213557754 and -0.0010403833570880039. The two-fit budget retained two named omissions without a ranking. Source fingerprint stayed unchanged across 332 read-only files. Both recursive generations promoted through existing gates and both replayed on resume with the same final checkpoint. Git was absent from PATH. Behavioral revert in a disposable copy removed training-slice membership effects: the deterministic movement test failed 0/1, then restored behavior passed 1/1. See docs/training-influence-evidence.json and docs/training-influence-revert.json."
  "2026-10-29T09:02:33.251Z",codex-agent,"The captured tarball passed all five supported host acquisition modes on CLI 2026.10.28: npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx and project-local. Every mode ran with Git absent, returned two measured comparisons, preserved idempotent retry, carried proposal evidence, and reported two omissions at a one-fit budget. Compact show output measured 1133 JSON bytes and 837 TOON bytes. Artifact contents and SHA-256 are recorded in docs/training-influence-packed.json. Stateful model validation uses pm test with pm_context_mode=none and workspace_context_mode=snapshot; after an expensive run was interrupted, redundant history/proposal replays were reduced while retaining all 500 SDK read-back sequences and all native fields/relationships in the model. Native SDK item creation arbitrates collisions; no lock-based isolation from workspace transactions is claimed, and the remaining post-read ordinary-writer window is documented."
  "2026-10-29T09:18:27.831Z",codex-agent,"Targeted native validation passed 7/7 via pm test --run --progress in a non-git snapshot workspace: all 500 seeded operation sequences completed and read state back through the SDK, including old-input replays, CRLF/whitespace, native annotations, relationships, custom status ids and ambient focus. Real SDK peers were injected at every measured read/write boundary for report creation and proposal feedback. An additional latest boundary run passed 3/3, including signed-zero normalization through the producer JSON wire format and malformed emitted-number refusals. Typecheck, test compilation and lint passed; duplicate and docstring gates passed without threshold changes. Final npm and Bun full-gate evidence will come from CI on the PR head, with URLs/counts recorded in the PR to keep tracker writes complete before final-head verification."
  "2026-10-29T09:40:37.358Z",codex-agent,"Final captured artifact passed all five npm/Bun global, ephemeral and local installation modes with Git absent. SHA-256 e68d259465fadd8ada8aab58374d7c177d59c83db03a7f3bf2ff36cf5a22d695, 816499 bytes; contents include the typed SDK module, CLI, example and documentation. SDK source-copy validation was independently compared byte-for-byte with all 332 tracker files at the declared public commit. Isolated strict tracker health passes; the existing development extension skew and legacy advisories are recorded on pm-rl-9uz4. Releasing this agent claim for ready-PR handoff; leave the feature open for orchestrator verification. Final-head full npm and Bun CI run URL/counts will be recorded in the PR, with no later tracker writes."
  "2026-10-29T09:53:43.047Z",codex-agent,"Final SDK contract inspection found that compact history index is a physical row position, while version is the durable address after native compaction (HistoryDiffEntry.version and HistoryResult.version_addressing). Correcting report citations to prefer version with an un-compacted index fallback; adding a real SDK compaction fixture and a durable-version oracle. Only new disposable fixture history is compacted; repository histories remain byte-prefix extensions. This is a package compatibility correction, not an SDK gap."
  "2026-10-29T10:07:39.067Z",codex-agent,"Durable-version compatibility regression passed 1/1 on a new non-git SDK fixture after native compaction. The independent oracle is HistoryResult.version_addressing.last_version. Reverting only readTrainingInfluence to physical row indices fails 0/1; restored behavior passes 1/1. The original training-slice behavioral revert also still fails 0/1 and restores 1/1. Updated artifact 77167abc786e877a710036fe2a98827991333fd850a0f7e553016c702826bc8d (816521 bytes) passed all five complete packed acquisition modes. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, duplicate and docstring checks pass. This correction supersedes the earlier frozen head and requires fresh final-head CI; final URL/counts remain in PR 119. No tracked history was compacted or rewritten."
  "2026-10-29T10:39:04.942Z",codex-agent,"Required final-head CI monitoring cutoff reached after 30 minutes for implementation head 5d7477a7a18b320dcf2d4466ccb6b872f57186b2. Run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/40855159641 still has test (22), test (26) and Bun release (26) queued: 0/3 release jobs completed, no final-head test or coverage totals available. This is pending evidence, not approval. Earlier run 40851706089 was superseded and canceled after the durable-version correction. This tracking-only receipt changes no implementation or packaged bytes; its push may queue a further check run. Leave the item open and the agent claim released. The orchestrator must wait for exact-head npm/Bun gates before closing or merging."
